Z||000000||fiero56||01-07-2001||10:14 PM||||I found a cheap sand/media/etc blaster. All I need it to do is to strip the c/c and paint off of 5 diamond spoke wheels. I've given up on chemical strippers and blasting the wheels would be easier anyway(I hope). I've got an air compressor, hosing, etc. The kit I found comes with the gun, the pickup, reservoir, everything expept the media. My question is will a setup like this remove the paint and clear coat from wheels? What type of media would be suggested? How much does it typically go for? <P>If this setup will work, I'll start making up a box this week.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-07-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||zeusrekning||01-07-2001||10:28 PM||||At work we use a bead blaster. We run about 90 p.s.i. of air pressure and it works great if the machine is not clogged or if the air does not have condensation in it.||||reg||1
